<https://citekg.org/resource/citation/8a9d22295eb28701/44> <https://citekg.org/ontology/hasContextBefore> "model. On the one hand, the main issue in a multi-agent distributed task is not the algorithms themselves, but the most appropriate mechanism to allow agents to collaborate, as said by Gorodetsky et al. [cite]. In this aspect, the argumentation technique applied the PISA framework [cite], providing a satisfactory collaboration mechanism. On the other hand, our diagnosis system deals with uncertain information and would need agents able to discuss those uncertain variables given a complete probability distribution about any unknown attribute of the diagnosis case using the soft-evidence technique"@en .
